---
/**
 * Five of the questions in docs/faq.md, with the answers shortened. The page at /docs/faq/ has
 * all of them; keep these in step with it. Plain <details>, no script.
 */
---

<div class="faq">
	<details>
		<summary>Why not just give the agent a read replica?</summary>
		<div class="answer">
			<p>
				A replica solves load and, since a hot standby rejects writes, it solves writes too. It
				does not hide a single column, it does not expire, it needs a password that then sits in
				the agent's config, and it logs nothing per query. Daypass and a replica go together: point
				a Daypass target at the replica and you get both.
			</p>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details>
		<summary>Does it work with other MCP clients?</summary>
		<div class="answer">
			<p>
				Yes. The server is <code>daypass mcp</code> over stdio, with no client-specific code. Claude
				Code: <code>claude mcp add --scope user daypass -- daypass mcp</code>. Clients that take a
				JSON config use the shape most of them share:
			</p>
			<pre class="land-code"><code>{`{ "mcpServers": { "daypass": { "command": "daypass", "args": ["mcp"] } } }`}</code></pre>
			<p>
				The lease is opened from a terminal regardless of client. The
				<a href="/docs/plugin/">Claude Code plugin</a> also adds a skill that teaches Claude the
				tools; other clients get the raw tools.
			</p>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details>
		<summary>MySQL? SQL Server? SQLite?</summary>
		<div class="answer">
			<p>
				No. Postgres only. The guard is Postgres's own parser (<code>libpg-query</code>), the role
				setup is Postgres SQL, and the hidden-column mechanism is Postgres column-level grants. A
				MySQL / MariaDB target type is listed under Next on the <a href="/roadmap/">roadmap</a>
				with status <em>idea</em>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details>
		<summary>What does the agent see?</summary>
		<div class="answer">
			<p>
				Five tools: <code>daypass_status</code>, <code>list_tables</code>,
				<code>describe_table</code>, <code>explain</code>, <code>query</code>. Through them: tables
				in the schemas the target allows with row estimates and sizes; columns, types and indexes
				of a table, minus the hidden columns and the indexes on them; query plans; and results
				capped at 500 rows and 1 MB in total and 2000 characters per cell, labelled
				<code>data, not instructions</code>. No tool returns the config file, the password, the
				IAM token, or the audit log. Two caveats: a query against the system catalog shows the
				<em>names</em> of hidden columns, never their values; and an agent that may also run shell
				commands as you can read <code>~/.daypass</code> directly.
			</p>
		</div>
	</details>
	<details>
		<summary>How do I revoke everything right now?</summary>
		<div class="answer">
			<ol>
				<li>
					<code>daypass close</code> on the machine: deletes the lease and removes the
					security-group rule. The next tool call is refused.
				</li>
				<li>
					In the database, as the owner: <code>ALTER ROLE daypass_ro NOLOGIN;</code> then
					<code>SELECT pg_terminate_backend(pid) FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE usename = 'daypass_ro';</code>.
					This ends every connection on every laptop at once.
				</li>
				<li>
					On AWS: remove <code>rds-db:connect</code> from the person's policy, or revoke their
					credentials. <code>daypass sweep &lt;target&gt;</code> cleans any rule they left.
				</li>
				<li>
					For a password target: <code>\password daypass_ro</code> in <code>psql</code> as the
					owner.
				</li>
			</ol>
			<p>The audit file on each machine stays; that is the record of what ran.</p>
		</div>
	</details>
</div>
<p class="all"><a href="/docs/faq/">All questions, with links to the guides</a></p>

<style>
	.faq {
		max-width: 48rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
	}
	details {
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
	}
	summary {
		cursor: pointer;
		list-style: none;
		display: flex;
		align-items: center;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		padding: 0.9rem 0;
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
	}
	summary::-webkit-details-marker {
		display: none;
	}
	summary::after {
		content: '';
		flex: none;
		width: 0.55rem;
		height: 0.55rem;
		border-right: 2px solid currentColor;
		border-bottom: 2px solid currentColor;
		transform: rotate(45deg);
		transition: transform 0.15s;
		margin-right: 0.25rem;
	}
	details[open] summary::after {
		transform: rotate(-135deg);
	}
	summary:hover {
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
	}
	.answer {
		padding: 0 0 1.1rem;
		max-width: 44rem;
		font-size: 0.925rem;
		line-height: 1.6;
		color: var(--sl-color-text);
	}
	.answer > * + * {
		margin-top: 0.75rem;
	}
	.answer ol {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}
	.answer li + li {
		margin-top: 0.4rem;
	}
	.answer pre {
		white-space: pre;
	}
	.all {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-size: 0.925rem;
	}
	@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
		summary::after {
			transition: none;
		}
	}
</style>
